$wide g = phi.alt pi \|_S \, wide h = g p_H .$

Only the support spaces in the left column map to $U$.

#thm([Lemma 7.4.])[
  (Residue with residual poles).  #emph[For every $i gt.eq 0$, the fixed adjoint isomorphism gives a split injection
#[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(7.7)")
 $ R^i g_(*) cal(O)_S \( a S \) arrow.r.hook R^i h_(*) omega_H \( A \) . $ <signed:residue-injection>]

 The injection and its retraction commute with the root germ comparisons.
   Under a product with a manifold they are the relative canonical constructions;
